sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User (tenant A)
  participant G as API Gateway
  participant T as Token Service
  participant O as Orders
  participant B as Billing
  participant L as Ledger
  U->>G: 1. request, with user token
  G->>G: 2. validate token: user and tenant proven
  G->>T: 3. token exchange (RFC 8693)
  T-->>G: 4. transaction token: caller, tenant, context
  G->>O: 5. internal call + transaction token
  O->>O: 6. verify token, authorize the caller
  O->>B: 7. charge account + transaction token
  B->>B: 8. verify token, derive tenant from token
  B->>L: 9. write entry + transaction token
  L->>L: 10. verify token, policy check on the verified caller
  Note over G,L: mTLS proves the channel, the token proves the caller: both, at every hop
  Note over B,L: tenant_id comes from the verified token,<br/>never from the request body
